  {
   "type": "text",
   "title": "",
   "options": {
    "mode": "markdown",
    "content": "**What you are looking at:** a simulated packaging line (press-01 &rarr; cnc-02 &rarr; robot-03) streaming telemetry over **MQTT** into **Node-RED**, which raises alerts and stores everything in **InfluxDB**. Every panel here is an InfluxDB query.\nInject a fault and watch the machine's signal climb, its health drop, alerts appear and, when a machine stops, the machines after it go **STARVED**.\n\n| Inject faults from | |\n|---|---|\n| **Control room** (buttons, scenarios, terminal, live MQTT feed) | [http://__PUBLIC_HOST__:__NODERED_PORT__/control](http://__PUBLIC_HOST__:__NODERED_PORT__/control) |\n| **MQTTX Web** (any MQTT client) | [http://__PUBLIC_HOST__:__MQTTX_PORT__](http://__PUBLIC_HOST__:__MQTTX_PORT__) &rarr; connect `ws://__PUBLIC_HOST__:__MQTT_WS_PORT__/mqtt`, publish `{\"fault\":\"overheat\"}` to `factory/__FACTORY_SITE__/__FACTORY_LINE__/press-01/cmd` |\n| **Node-RED editor** (Fault Injection tab) | [http://__PUBLIC_HOST__:__NODERED_PORT__](http://__PUBLIC_HOST__:__NODERED_PORT__) |\n\nFaults: press-01 `overheat`, `hydraulic_leak` &middot; cnc-02 `bearing`, `tool_wear` (3 hits stop it) &middot; robot-03 `jam`, `misgrip` (3 in 2 min trip it) &middot; `none` clears. Chaos mode: `on`/`off` to `factory/__FACTORY_SITE__/__FACTORY_LINE__/chaos`. All logins use the stack admin credentials."
   },
   "datasource": {
    "type": "grafana",
    "uid": "grafana"
   },
   "id": 2,
   "gridPos": {
    "x": 0,
    "y": 1,
    "w": 24,
    "h": 7
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "row",
   "title": "Line status",
   "collapsed": false,
   "panels": [],
